<%#
  The plugin's settings screen (WP5).

  Two settings, both counted in workflow rules and both about the same thing
  from opposite ends (WP13): above the first, an action asks; above the second,
  an administration matrix save is refused outright. Rendered by Redmine inside
  its own box.tabular.settings, so the markup is core's -- a label, a field and
  an em.info -- and the plugin adds no styling of its own.

  The field shows the number that is actually in force, not an empty box, so an
  administrator who saves this page without touching it keeps what was there.
%>
<p>
  <label for="settings_bulk_confirm_threshold">
    <%= l(:label_project_workflow_bulk_confirm_threshold) %>
  </label>
  <%# type=number with a floor of zero, because Redmine's plugin settings have
      no validation hook: SettingsController#plugin assigns the hash as it
      arrives. The helper still falls back to the default for anything that is
      not a run of digits -- that is what answers for a value saved before this
      attribute was here, or by a client that ignores it -- but the field now
      refuses to submit one instead of accepting it and silently ignoring it. %>
  <%= text_field_tag 'settings[bulk_confirm_threshold]',
                     settings['bulk_confirm_threshold'].presence ||
                       RedmineProjectWorkflows::BulkActionsHelper::DEFAULT_BULK_CONFIRM_THRESHOLD,
                     id: 'settings_bulk_confirm_threshold', size: 6,
                     type: 'number', min: 0, step: 1 %>
  <em class="info"><%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_confirm_threshold) %></em>
</p>

<p>
  <label for="settings_bulk_write_ceiling">
    <%= l(:label_project_workflow_bulk_write_ceiling) %>
  </label>
  <%# Same shape as the field above, and the same reason for type=number: Redmine
      assigns the plugin settings hash exactly as it arrives, so the fallback in
      Services::WriteBudget is what answers for anything that is not a run of
      digits and this attribute is what stops one being submitted. %>
  <%= text_field_tag 'settings[bulk_write_ceiling]',
                     settings['bulk_write_ceiling'].presence ||
                       RedmineProjectWorkflows::Services::WriteBudget::DEFAULT_WRITE_CEILING,
                     id: 'settings_bulk_write_ceiling', size: 8,
                     type: 'number', min: 0, step: 1 %>
  <em class="info"><%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_write_ceiling) %></em>
</p>
